The result of a community evaluation is usually "each model's score on a set of questions". Write two functions that aggregate those into a leaderboard.

`rank(models)`:

- `models` is a dict whose keys are model names and whose values are that model's list of per-question scores (numbers from 0 to 100);
- an empty score list averages to `0.0`; otherwise the average is the sum of the scores divided by the number of questions, **rounded to 1 decimal place**;
- it returns a list of `{'name': model name, 'avg': average}`, sorted by average **from high to low**, and on equal averages by model name in **lexicographic order**.

`best_model(models)`: returns the name of the first row of the leaderboard; returns `None` when `models` is empty (or when every model has no scores and they all tie).

